2026-07-11 (mcp_tool command landed: isar-level tool registration)
-------------------------------------------------------------------

- implemented plans/mcp_tool_command on top of the registry pivot
  (below): the mcp_tool / mcp_resource / mcp_test keywords and
  commands in MCP_Tools.thy. mcp_tool wraps a diagnostic command
  (registration-time Outer_Syntax.check_command + Keyword.is_diag,
  position-reported for ctrl+click) with optional (description ...)
  (params name :: type [= default] <descr> ...) (format <...>)
  clauses, or takes the ML hatches (= <string -> string>, = run
  <full-power fn with declared params>); mcp_resource takes a bare
  fact name (pretty-printed at READ time, so dynamic collections
  stay current), (isar <diagnostic text>) captured output, or an ML
  read function. mcp_test is a reserved stub (its wave later).
- the layer underneath: MCP_Combinators (closed param-type universe
  string/source/args/nat/int/bool/term/typ/fact; type-directed
  quoting where adversarial values stay data — pinned by injection
  tests; validation with typed errors naming the argument; format
  assembly; execution by parsing at Position.line 1 and folding
  Toplevel.command_exception over a throwaway state of the RUN
  context's theory, output captured, multiline payloads framed on
  their own line and reported line numbers shifted back to "line N-1
  of your input"). the capture substrate moved from MCP_Repl.thy to
  MCP_Tools.thy as MCP_Output (the two phase-2 output-routing test
  boxes are closed in MCP-HOL-Tests); MCP_Repl now builds on it.
- TWO SURFACE CORRECTIONS forced by the outer lexer (command
  keywords delimit command spans, so they cannot appear as inner
  tokens anywhere): wrapped command names are quoted (mcp_tool
  "find_consts"), and the activation attribute is plural
  ([[mcp_tools add: ...]] / [[mcp_resources ...]]). also pinned:
  description is MANDATORY for tools (Outer_Syntax stores but does
  not export command comments), and the default input of a bare diag
  wrap has the new type "args" (verbatim splice into the command's
  argument position — quoting it would break the command's own
  argument syntax).
- schema over the bridge: rows carry declared params (yxml);
  MCP.run_tool takes named args (the MCP.ir encoding); scala expands
  params to JSON schemas (nat/int -> integer, bool -> boolean, rest
  string with the validation contract in the description; defaults
  typed) and diag_wrap advertises readOnly+idempotent annotations.
  tools/call forwards all JSON arguments as named pairs; ML
  validation owns missing/ill-typed errors.
- listChanged closed end to end (the phase-2 builtin-table item's
  last open half): declare emits MCP.tools_changed/resources_changed,
  MCP_Session forwards through a callback, serve() pushes
  notifications/{tools,resources}/list_changed (stdout line-atomic),
  initialize declares the capability. e2e: test_mcp.py loads a
  fixture registering a tool with mcp_tool and observes the
  notification (60 verdicts, 0 failures; all unit/bridge/heap suites
  green).
- deferred: enum/list param types, the (scoped) modifier, HOL first
  user (value), tools/list of runtime-registered tools (needs
  plans/tool_scope designation control).

2026-07-11 (registry pivot LANDED: tools are context entities)
---------------------------------------------------------------

- implemented plans/mcp_tool_registry (spec phase 3 "the pivot",
  first item of the implementation order, now checked): MCP_Tool and
  MCP_Resource left the global Synchronized.var and became context
  entities — a shared MCP_Registry ML functor holding a Name_Space
  table (definitions: positions/ctrl+click, completion,
  theory-qualified names) plus a Symtab.set (activation) in
  Generic_Data, both merging by union (pinned by the fixture
  diamond). MCP_Tool.declare is the one entry point (register is
  gone; grep gate clean); tools declare with a form tag
  (string_fun/diag_wrap/method_wrap), a param-list placeholder and a
