  print_mcp_resources ("!" = include inactive) print with entity
  markup.
- protocol commands MCP.tools/run_tool/resources/read_resource carry
  a DESIGNATION argument (canonical theory long name; "" = the
  MCP_Tools theory itself); rows cross the bridge under FULL internal
  names + form tag, and the scala side computes exposed names
  (MCP_Server.exposure: base name when unambiguous and not a builtin,
  else sanitized qualified name, dots -> "__"; colliding entries
  dropped, never shadowing) — pulled forward from plans/tool_scope
  because the client-name contract needed it the moment qualified
  names crossed. tools/call and resources/read resolve back through
  the same map.
- duplicate declare in one theory now errors (Name_Space strict) —
  the mvp replace-by-name idempotence test replaced accordingly;
  registration order is no longer a served-order guarantee
  (Name_Space.dest_table sorts).
- test surface: MCP-Tools-Tests gained fixture theories (visibility
  follows imports, sibling isolation, del/add diamond, bundle
  open/close); scala unit suites cover exposure; the bridge suite
  covers explicit-vs-default designation and typed unknown-
  designation errors; a new MCP_Registry_Heap_Tests pins heap
  survival of registration+activation from a fresh ML_process (via
  ML_Context.eval_in — theory-defined ML structures are not bound at
  the raw ML_process toplevel); test_mcp.py green at 58/58 with
  unchanged client-visible names ("shout", isabelle://named/
  greeting). declare emits MCP.tools_changed (dropped outside
  PIDE/server); scala forwarding of listChanged remains with
  plans/mcp_tool_command step 5.

