  protocol_message-from-futures (already proven by MCP_Repl.thy's ir
  emit + green bridge tests); Name_Space-in-Generic_Data
  (define/check/extern, completion errors, recorded positions).
- two spec CORRECTIONS from the spikes: (1) ML_val/snippet errors —
  text parsed at Position.none carries NO positions; the diag_wrap
  runner must parse at Position.line 1, which yields exact
  snippet-relative lines (verified with a line-100 offset datum);
  spec section "snippet evaluation" rewritten accordingly. (2)
  eisbach schema derivation DEMOTED: METHOD_CLOSURE does not export
  its closure data, so mcp_tool (method) on eisbach methods gets the
  generic {repl, args} schema unless an explicit params clause is
  given; automatic derivation parked behind an upstream signature
  extension. also added: the exposure-name caveat (extern'd names
  keep dots; the phase-2 sanitizer survives the pivot).
- wrote the first three phase-3 implementation plans:
  plans/mcp_tool_registry (the Generic_Data + Name_Space pivot,
  attribute, print_mcp_tools, compat wrapper, designation argument on
  the protocol commands; zero client-visible change gate),
  plans/tool_scope (agent-context designation state, the three
  tool_scope_* builtin rows, exposure-name function = extern
  shortening + sanitizer, the repl-designation self-extension hinge),
  plans/mcp_tool_command (params/format language + type-directed
  quoting + MCP_Combinators + exec-at-position runner; absorbs and
  closes phase 2's open mcp_tool/mcp_resource outer-syntax item and
  the tools_changed forwarding). plans/README notes the phase-3
  family-plan convention.

2026-07-11 (phase 3 spec: isar-level extensibility)
----------------------------------------------------

- new spec section "phase 3 — isar-level extensibility (tools as
  context entities)", the brainstorm-to-spec pass for the
  user-extensibility story beyond wave 3. decisions, all grounded in
  existing isabelle mechanisms (named_theorems.ML as the package
  model, bundle.ML for scoping, simproc's declare [[...del:]]
  attribute precedent, eisbach method closures, entity_antiquotation
  patterns):
  * the pivot: MCP_Tool/MCP_Resource move from a global
    Synchronized.var to a Name_Space table in Generic_Data —
    positions/ctrl+click/completion/qualified names/import-following
    visibility for free; phase 2's bespoke collision scheme reduces
    to Name_Space extern.
  * visibility split into registration (name space, unconditional)
    vs activation (name set + declare [[mcp_tool add/del: name]]);
    bundles scope tools with zero new machinery; the server reads
    everything relative to a designated AGENT CONTEXT (theory or
    repl; new tool_scope_show/set/include builtins, distinct from
    the phase-2 resource scope).
  * a closed declarative params clause (types incl. term/typ/fact
    with server-side validation, defaults, enums, per-param docs) +
    type-directed-quoting format clause = the tool specification
    language; json schemas derived scala-side from serialized
    descriptors; MCP_Combinators as the ML layer under the sugar.
  * payoff inventory verified by grep: every :: diag command wraps
    for one line — Pure/HOL (find_theorems, value, quickcheck,
    nitpick, sledgehammer, ML_val...) and AFP entries' own
    print_*/find_*/try_* commands.
  * ML_val wrapping = snippet evaluation with compiler errors;
    position normalization into the user's snippet specced.
  * methods via method_wrap (repl-stepping apply); eisbach needs no
    wrapping for agent-authored automation (method is a local_theory
    command, repl_step handles it) but donates schema derivation
    from its declarative headers.
  * mcp_test command: declaration-time tests (build = test runner),
    slow tags behind a config option, recorded suite rerunnable via
    the mcp_test_run diag command (itself a tool — the agent tests
    its own tools live).
  * explorability: context-relative ML api, print_mcp_tools,
    \<^mcp_tool> ML antiquotation, @{mcp_tool}/@{mcp_tool_schema}
    document antiquotations with rendering options.
  * the self-extension loop documented as the composition of the
    above (no dedicated feature).
  * skills impact assessed in-spec: isabelle-ml gains
    bundles/eisbach/document-antiquotation/keyword topics;
    isabelle-ml-scala gets the bridge-encoding delta; new skill
    isabelle-mcp-extending planned; additions queued for the three
    planned phase-2 skills.

