2026-07-10 (isabelle://named/{name}: MCP_Resource registry)
----------------------------------------------------------------------

- done: backed isabelle://named/{name}, the last of the seven
  documented resource templates without at least a real backing path.
  Added MCP_Resource to MCP_Tools.thy, a structure/registry mirroring
  MCP_Tool exactly (register from a plain ML block; no new outer-syntax
  mcp_resource command yet -- that sugar is separate future work
  tracked in the spec's "mcp_tool / mcp_resource outer syntax commands"
  checklist item, and isn't needed for the registry+protocol mechanism
  itself to work, the same way MCP_Tool has functioned without an
  mcp_tool command all along). New protocol commands MCP.resources
  (list, mirrors MCP.theories) and MCP.read_resource (id-keyed read,
  mirrors MCP.run_tool). Scala side: MCP_Session.ml_named_resources/
  ml_read_resource (new promise plumbing, same pattern as
  ml_tools/ml_run); mcp_resources() now merges isabelle://session with
  one isabelle://named/{name} entry per registered resource;
  mcp_resource_read dispatches isabelle://named/{name} straight to
  ml_read_resource. Demo resource "greeting" registered alongside the
  existing "shout" demo tool, for tests.
- tests, all three non-ml layers: bridge (mcp_bridge_tests.scala,
  "bridge: ml_named_resources ...", "... ml_read_resource ...", "...
  mcp_resources lists isabelle://named/greeting ...", "... resources/
  read dispatches to MCP_Resource" -- all against a real MCP-Tools
  session, genuinely round-tripping through the registry); scala unit
  (mcp_handler_tests.scala, Fake_Backend's named_resources field
  mirrors extra_ml_tools); e2e (test_mcp.py, "resources/list includes
  isabelle://named/greeting" + the read/unknown-name cases).
- bugfix along the way: an edit that dropped not_yet_backed_uri's
  wrapping capture group (while narrowing it to no longer need the
  isabelle://named/{name} alternative, now dispatched separately)
  silently broke the fallback -- `case not_yet_backed_uri(_)` needs
  exactly one regex group to bind, and a 0-group Regex extractor
  matches nothing, ever. Caught immediately by the existing "non-image
  ... still not backed" bridge test failing with a bare "Unknown MCP
  resource" instead of the documented-gap message. Fixed by keeping
  the outer capturing group even though its content isn't used
  (`case not_yet_backed_uri(_)`); mcp_session.scala and mcp_testing.
  scala both had the same regex, both fixed. Lesson: a Scala Regex
  extractor's case arity must match its actual group count exactly --
  removing an alternative from inside a capturing group is safe, but
  removing the group itself while keeping a binding pattern in the
  case is not.
- resource-template scorecard, all 7 now backed for at least their
  reachable scope: isabelle://repl/{id} and .../text (thin ir bridge
  dispatch); isabelle://theory/{name}/diagnostics (three-tier: image/
  loaded/filesystem); isabelle://theory/{name} bare and .../commands
  (image tier, via Ir.source/source_map); isabelle://theory/{name}/
  entities (image tier via Name_Space, loaded tier via PIDE entity-def
  markup); isabelle://named/{name} (this entry). Remaining gaps are
  narrower than "unbacked template": filesystem-tier theory/{name},
  /commands and /entities still need wave 3 (session-structure path
  resolution) for theories never loaded into any running session; the
  outer-syntax mcp_resource command sugar (not the registry) is
  separate future polish.

2026-07-10 (entities name qualification; MCP_Heap_Suite)
----------------------------------------------------------------------

- diagnosed the one issue found implementing isabelle://theory/{name}/
  entities: name qualification. The scala image_tier gate accepts both
  base and session-qualified theory names but forwards the client's
  original string to ML, where Thy_Info.get_theory does an exact-key
  lookup against a table that mixes qualified and unqualified keys
  ("HOL.Wellfounded" but plain "Main"). Live matrix and fix direction
  (pass the resolved qualified name from scala, or resolve base names
  in ML against Thy_Info.get_names) recorded in plans/find_definition's
  entities section. Also verified there: the heap-survival assumption
  HOLDS — Thy_Info.get_theory and name-space entry positions survive a
  fresh process from a saved heap; entities is NOT the segments gap.
- new test fixture MCP_Heap_Suite (mcp_test/src/mcp_testing.scala):
  raw ML run by a fresh `isabelle ML_process` against a saved heap
  (ml/ml_check/ml_test; suites in mcp_test/src/mcp_heap_tests.scala,
  run under `isabelle mcp_test -b`). Covers fresh-process/heap-restart
  claims — the environment build-time \<^assert> theories can never
  test, and the class both the segments gap and the Thy_Info keying
  issue belong to. Infrastructure + fixture self-test only so far; no
  ML tests migrated. See plans/README "testing process".
- FIXED (same day, scala side): new mcp_session.scala image_theory
  resolver — client spelling -> canonical loaded_theories key
  (verbatim, then session-qualified, then unique base-name match;
  unknown/ambiguous -> not image tier), and the resolved name is what
  crosses the ir bridge. Applies uniformly to /entities, /commands,
  bare /theory/{name} (image_tier = image_theory(name).isDefined) and
  unload_theory's image check. All six rows of the plan's live matrix
  now answer correctly; pinned by the bridge test "wave 2 resources:
  ... entities -- image-tier names are normalized to the canonical
  Thy_Info key". Full mcp_test -b suite green.
- RETRACTED the segments KNOWN GAP (entry below, "resources:
  isabelle://theory/{name} source and commands"): it was FALSE, an
  artifact of this same name bug. The old flow forwarded the client's
  base spelling to ML; Thy_Info.get_theory errored "undefined entry";
  ir.ML's find_source swallowed that ERROR and rewrote it as "No
  recorded segments" -- which read exactly like a missing-segments
  condition. With the resolved canonical key, segments recorded at
  build time (record_theories, mcp/Tools/ROOT) DO survive the saved
  heap: isabelle://theory/MCP_Repl and .../commands return real source
  from a live server. The genuine error case is a heap built WITHOUT
  record_theories (stock HOL): still answers with Isabelle's rebuild
  hint. Bridge test rewritten as a positive pin (mcp_bridge_tests.
  scala "recorded segments survive into the live server"); e2e updated
  (MCP_Repl/commands ok + Main/commands still the rebuild hint);
  comments corrected in mcp_session.scala and MCP_Repl.thy. NOTE:
  Ir.load_theory's own headless refusal is a separate, still-real gap.

2026-07-10 (resources: isabelle://theory/{name} source and commands)
----------------------------------------------------------------------

- attempted, found a KNOWN GAP: wired isabelle://theory/{name} (bare,
  source) and isabelle://theory/{name}/commands to the already-existing
  MCP.ir fnames "source"/"source_map" (Ir.source/Ir.source_map,
  mcp/Tools/HOL/ir.ML), gated on the theory being image-tier
  (session.resources.loaded_theory). Empirically, this never succeeds
  against a live `isabelle mcp_server` process, for ANY theory,
  including the session's own -T theory: Ir.source/source_map read off
  Thy_Info.get_theory_segments, which turns out to be populated only
  within the process that actually ran `isabelle build` with
  record_theories -- it does not survive into a freshly started process
  even against the SAME saved heap (unlike Document.Node data, which
  the heap itself serializes). A session-wide variant of the existing
  Ir.load_theory KNOWN GAP (Ir.load_theory refuses in headless
  sessions; this is broader — no theory's segments are reachable from a
  live server at all, image-tier or not).
- decision: kept the dispatch wired anyway (mcp_session.scala's
  theory_source_uri/theory_commands_uri, gated on image_tier) rather
  than falling back to the generic not_yet_backed_uri message, because
  it surfaces Isabelle's own specific, actionable error ("No recorded
  segments for X. Rebuild the session heap with: isabelle build -o
  record_theories=true -b <SESSION>") instead of a bare "documented
  template, not backed yet" — and the routing itself is the correct
  logic a future fix to the segments gap would benefit from immediately.
  Non-image (wave-2-loaded or filesystem) theories still fall through
  to not_yet_backed_uri, since they were never going to have segments
  either way.
- tests, pinning the gap rather than hiding it: bridge
  (mcp_bridge_tests.scala, "wave 2 resources: ... KNOWN GAP: recorded
  segments don't survive a fresh headless process, even for the
  session's own -T theory" — MCP_Repl itself, not just Main, still
  errors), scala unit (mcp_handler_tests.scala, dispatch-routing only,
  explicit in its name and comment that it does not claim production
  success), e2e (test_mcp.py, "... KNOWN GAP names the real reason").
- isabelle://theory/{name}/entities and isabelle://named/{name} remain
  fully unbacked (not_yet_backed_uri) — entities needs its own
  navigation infra (find_definition/goto_definition, a separate
  checklist item), named needs the unbuilt mcp_tool/mcp_resource ML
  outer-syntax commands, neither touched this round.

