  (isabelle://theory/*, isabelle://named/{name}) return a distinct
  "documented template, not backed yet (needs a later implementation
  wave)" error rather than the generic "Unknown MCP resource" — the
  same don't-pretend-it-works honesty already used for the
  load_theory KNOWN GAP, so a client (or a human reading the error)
  learns this is a known, tracked gap and not a typo'd uri.
  resources/list itself is untouched (still just isabelle://session,
  concretely listed) — pagination cursor and uri query-parameter
