2026-07-10 (later)
-------------------

- done: find_theorems implemented (plans/find_theorems, wave 1 — the
  last builtin tool of wave 1's proof-search family) — builtin table
  row (fname "find_theorems", {readOnlyHint: true, idempotentHint:
  true} -- pure search); optional max_results property (default 40),
  same omission mechanism as sledgehammer's timeout_secs.
- decided: mcp_server.py's python-side query auto-quoting heuristic
  (bare term patterns silently wrapped in quotes) is deliberately NOT
  reimplemented scala-side — the tool description teaches the quoting
  contract instead (name patterns unquoted, term/simp patterns
  quoted). T5 (e2e) confirmed the contract is livable as stated:
  name:conjI and "_ + _ = _ + _" both return hits through the full
  stack without any auto-quoting.
- fixed/pinned: a genuine, previously-undocumented shape in
  Find_Theorems.find_theorems_cmd's return value, found while writing
  T3. It returns opt_found = NONE whenever a max_results limit cuts
  the search short (the exhaustive total is unknown at that point),
  so a BOUNDED query's tally is "displaying N theorem(s)", never
  "found N theorem(s) (M displayed)" as ir.ML's own tally-formatting
  code might suggest in isolation — that found/displayed split only
  fires when the search is unlimited (max_results 0) and completes
  exhaustively. Pinned with "name:conj" against Main (more than 3
  matches): max_results=3 truncates to "displaying 3 theorem(s)",
  max_results=0 returns the full "found N theorem(s)" count. T2
  confirmed a malformed query (unterminated quote) is a clean status
  error, not a crash. T4 confirmed goal-based criteria ("intro") error
  cleanly at theory level with no goal, and return plausible rules
  (conjI) once mid-proof on a conjunction goal. T6 confirmed
  find_theorems on one REPL returns promptly during a slow step on a
  different REPL — no async gymnastics of its own, but it does not
  queue behind an unrelated slow call either.
  ml unit: MCP_Repl_Tests.thy; scala unit: isabelle mcp_test; bridge
