- done: repl_pin, repl_unpin, and repl_rebase implemented together
  (plans/repl_pin, plans/repl_unpin, plans/repl_rebase, wave 1 — the
  pin/rebase composition feature) — three builtin table rows: repl_pin
  (fname "pin", {readOnlyHint: false, idempotentHint: false} -- each
  call bumps the pin version, not a no-op), repl_unpin (fname "unpin",
  same non-idempotent mutating shape -- unpinning an unpinned REPL
  errors), repl_rebase (fname "rebase", {idempotentHint: true} -- a
  REPL already on the latest pins replies "already up to date").
  repl_pin T1 confirmed pinning mid-proof is refused ("in a proof
  state"). T2 confirmed the round trip: A defines a constant and pins,
  B is init'd from ["pin@A"], B's origin literally prints "pin@A", and
  B can use A's definition immediately. T3 pinned the staleness trigger
  set: ANY successful with_claim-based mutation (step/edit/replay/
  rebase/merge) marks a REPL's pin stale on release regardless of what
  actually changed -- verified with a step that has nothing to do with
  the pinned content -- and a new init from a stale pin errors while
  existing dependents are untouched; re-pinning clears it. T4 confirmed
  re-pinning twice both succeed. repl_unpin T1 confirmed unpinning an
  unpinned REPL errors "is not pinned". T2 confirmed dependents block
  unpin (origin-spec based, so removing the dependent frees it, not
  rebasing it) and A's own steps are unchanged throughout. repl_rebase
  T1 exercised the whole point end to end: A gains a definition and
  re-pins, rebase B marks its steps stale, replay lets a NEW step in B
  use A's new definition, a second rebase says "already up to date".
  T2 confirmed a stale pin blocks rebase. T3 confirmed non-From_Theory
  origins (forks) are refused. T4 confirmed rebase does NOT replay --
  state is byte-identical pre/post rebase, only staleness and the base
  theory move. All three tools share one e2e fixture (repl_pin T5,
  repl_rebase T5, repl_unpin's e2e need): a build-a-base workflow
  against a live server -- PinA defines a constant and pins, PinB
