  concurrent-call handling, find_theorems auto-quoting dropped,
  literal scope_remove semantics).
- done: named-args migration (the "argument encoding" decision
  implemented). MCP_Repl.dispatch takes (key, value) pairs instead of
  positional strings — keys mirror mcp_server.py parameter names
  (repl, theories, isar_text, state_idx, ...), each fname owns a
  closed key set, missing/spurious/unparsable arguments are typed
  status errors naming the key, optional args keep their engine
  defaults (timeout_secs 15, max_results 40), list args as repeated
  keys (repl_init.theories). the MCP.ir protocol command decodes one
  yxml chunk via MCP_Repl.decode_args; scala mirror
  MCP_Session.encode_args/decode_args. tests: build-time self-test
  (dispatch + error paths + decode round-trip), scala unit round-trips
  in isabelle mcp_test; all layers green.
- added: plans/ — per-builtin-tool implementation plans (metadata row,
  layer mapping, steps, assumptions each with its test in the pyramid).
  plans/README carries the template and the wave-ordered index; pilot
  plan: plans/repl_list, which also states the shared infrastructure
  assumptions I1..I5 that later plans reference. flags one spec
  refinement: repl_list (and the other read-only repl_* tools) should
  get readOnlyHint true despite the spec's coarse repl_* blanket.
- decided: advertised tool/resource metadata. tools: name + inputSchema
  required (json schema, top-level object, common subset); description
  always sent (outer-syntax comment default for wrapped commands);
  honest annotations (readOnlyHint/idempotentHint on diagnostic wraps,
  readOnly builtins except the mutating surface); no outputSchema in
  phase 2 (text results only); no examples slot exists in the protocol
  — examples ride in descriptions/skills. schemas are static per tool,
  fixed by the registration form: ML registry carries a form tag
  (diag_wrap | string_fun) expanded to schema + annotations scala-side;
  MCP.tools payload becomes (name, description, theory, form_tag)
  quadruples. resources: uri + name required; we add description,
  mimeType text/plain, audience ["assistant"]; size/lastModified
  deliberately absent (read-time evaluation). spec: "mcp tools" ->
  "advertised tool metadata"; "mcp resources" -> "advertised resource
  metadata".
- decided: MCP.ir argument encoding is named args in yxml — args =
  [id, fname, yxml_args], where yxml_args is an association list of
  (key, value) string pairs, list-valued arguments as repeated keys.
  supersedes the positional-strings sketch; handles optional args
  (find_theorems.max_results, sledgehammer.timeout_secs) and list
  args (repl_init.theories) without arity variants or sentinels.
  spec: "ml bridge" -> "argument encoding".
- decided: tool name collisions resolve by namespacing with the
  registering theory — builtins keep the bare name; a colliding
  ML/Isar tool is exposed as <theory base name>__<tool> (escalating
  to the sanitized long name if base names collide). exposed names
  must match the messages-api constraint ^[a-zA-Z0-9_-]{1,64}$
  (theory long names contain dots, so they cannot appear raw).
  MCP.tools payload becomes (name, description, theory) triples;
  exposure names are computed scala-side as a pure function at the
  tools/list merge; registry replacement is keyed on (theory, name).
  spec: "mcp tools" -> "tool naming and collisions".
- added: implementation-plan mapping of the ~30 builtin tools to five
  backing mechanisms (MCP.ir bridge, use_theories, session-structure
  index, scope state, navigation) — discussion only, order unchanged.

